libpdfium (156.8078.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Update PDFium to chromium/8078 (Chromium 156.0.8078.47, 2f22dfe030de).
    - Meson: `core/fpdfapi/edit/cpdf_contentstream_write_utils.cpp` moved
      upstream to `core/fxcrt/stream_write_utils.cpp` (with its dragonbox
      dependency); the `fpdfapi_contentstream_write_utils` component is gone.
      Audit baseline updated.
    - ABI: compatible additions `FPDFAttachment_GetAFRelationship`,
      `FPDFPageObj_GetRenderedFillPattern`; SONAME stays `libpdfium.so.8059`.
  * Publish to the Valkyrian Labs APT repository (`release.toml`
    `repository_url` = `https://apt.valkyrianlabs.com`, Production
    `NEXUS_REPO_URL` likewise; apt.vaulthalla.sh is an alias of the same
    index); shared `valkyrianlabs-apt-publish` concurrency group; package tests
    read from apt.valkyrianlabs.com.

 -- Cooper Larson <cooper@valkyrianlabs.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:50:50 +0000

libpdfium (155.8059.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Build PDFium natively with Meson + Ninja from the official googlesource.com
    repository (chromium/8059, Chromium 155.0.8059.39); no CMake, GN, gclient
    or depot_tools.
  * Rename the runtime package to libpdfium8059 (SONAME libpdfium.so.8059) for
    the new ABI.
  * Export only the public C API (linker version script) and ship a symbols
    file.
  * Use system abseil, FreeType, HarfBuzz, ICU, lcms2, libjpeg and zlib; keep
    PDFium's bundled, patched AGG and OpenJPEG.
  * Include all predefined CJK CMaps (the legacy build disabled them).
  * Install fpdf_thumbnail.h and make the C++ helper headers usable from
    /usr/include/pdfium.
  * pdfium.pc adds -I${includedir}/pdfium; drop the -dev package's unneeded
    dependencies on other libraries' -dev packages.
  * Ship the upstream source lock (sources.lock.json) in the runtime package
    documentation.
  * Rewrite debian/copyright: exact PDFium, OpenJPEG, AGG, FreeType (FTL),
    fast_float and dragonbox notices with full license texts; test fonts are
    excluded from the source package and no test assets are installed.
  * Run the integration tests (rendering, text extraction, malformed input)
    during the build.

 -- Cooper Larson <cooper@valkyrianlabs.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:10:34 +0000
